# Hermes (extension layer) — environment reference

Runtime config lives in the official Hermes Agent's own files under
`~/.hermes/` (see AGENTS.md). This file documents the env vars this repo's
extension layer consumes. Nothing here is a runtime the repo ships.

## LLM (only provider — MiniMax-M3, D-D)

| Var | Where | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `MINIMAX_API_KEY` | `~/.hermes/.env` | `providers.minimax.api_key` |
| (model) | `~/.hermes/config.yaml` `model:` | provider `minimax`, model `MiniMax-M3`, `base_url https://api.minimax.chat/v1`, `api_mode chat_completions` |

## Discord (one token per profile, own secret scope)

| Var | Where | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN` | `~/.hermes/profiles/<name>/.env` | per-profile bot token (Main Agent default profile, assistant, tutor) |
| `DISCORD_ALLOWED_USERS` / `GATEWAY_ALLOWED_USERS` | same file | operator allowlist — zero public exposure |
| `DISCORD_HOME_CHANNEL` | operator config | home channel id (reference for enablement) |

Legacy token env names (`DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN_MAIN_AGENT`, `_ASSISTANT`,
`_TUTOR`) may exist on the VM from the archived private stack — migrate the
values, not the names.

## Memory infra (self-hosted, D-C)

| Var | Where | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `HONCHO_API_KEY` (optional) | `~/.hermes/.env` | Honcho provider key; local `baseUrl` auto-skips key auth |
| `baseUrl` | `~/.hermes/honcho.json` | `http://127.0.0.1:<port>` — self-hosted honcho-api |
| Ollama | 127.0.0.1:11434 | `nomic-embed-text`, 768-dim (setup/ollama/) |

## Codebase index

| Var | Where | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| indexer config | `~/.config/hermes-indexer/config.json` (NOT `~/.hermes/`) | sync allowlists etc. |
| MCP token | `~/.hermes/config.yaml` `mcp_servers.hermes-indexer` | Bearer token for the indexer MCP endpoint (Tailscale/127.0.0.1 bound) |